  "implementation": [
    "The existing same BookSourceFetcher instance is injected into DiscoverViewModel and forwarded to existing quick-action helpers. No runtime/state owner/store/body/category cache is created.",
    "Every eligible traditional category reload opens its existing original context before accepting a disk category cache hit. Failed/cancelled opens cannot publish cached categories or start sections.",
    "ExploreSourcePage appearance/disappearance forward lifecycle only. Existing layout, tokens, localized UI, presentations and previews are untouched.",
    "The same VM tracks category/section/automatic-controls/user-controls tasks. Leave invalidates publication token, cancels then awaits captured actual terminal tasks before per-source pending save. Repeat disappearance reuses its one pause task; rapid reentry waits the previous pause before its open/load.",
    "Page save resolves the current source by UUID, compares current rule/settings identity off main, and invokes the existing savePendingOriginalExploreContext through the same service. A failed/revised/removed source is logged without clearing or ACKing original needSave.",
    "Native JNI fixture uses the actual cached VM route, an original infoMap-dependent loopback explore request, actual pending cache absence, actual page-leave save and durable cache readback. The second disappearance must not advance the real cache revision.",
    "Cache characterization fixtures now replace only the native executor and await the returned load task instead of timing-based polling. The prior source-only no-native cache assumption no longer hides context initialization."
  ],
